battery: keep reporting while idle

The report timer stopped as soon as the keyboard went idle (30 s without a
key press), so the level a host showed froze, e.g. for the whole time the
keyboard sat charging.  Keep it running while idle and stop it only for
deep sleep.  Hosts are still only notified when the level changes.

Applies to petejohanson/zmk 5565f21.

diff --git a/app/src/battery.c b/app/src/battery.c
index 811baf8..00c2d82 100644
--- a/app/src/battery.c
+++ b/app/src/battery.c
@@ -168,7 +168,8 @@ static int battery_event_listener(const zmk_event_t *eh) {
         case ZMK_ACTIVITY_ACTIVE:
             zmk_battery_start_reporting();
             return 0;
         case ZMK_ACTIVITY_IDLE:
+            return 0;
         case ZMK_ACTIVITY_SLEEP:
             k_timer_stop(&battery_timer);
             return 0;
